MID_EV12_068_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_068_m01_019: By the gods! You're alive!
MID_EV12_068_m01_020: Ngh...
MID_EV12_068_m01_021: Alright there, feller?
MID_EV12_068_m01_022: <NCA>Remark on this unknown place.
MID_EV12_068_m01_023: I do not know this place.
MID_EV12_068_m01_024: Strange way to put it. Sounds like you're a fish\nout of water, maybe?
MID_EV12_068_m01_025: You're on an ordinary beach in Dagda!
MID_EV12_068_m01_026: I am? Truly?
MID_EV12_068_m01_027: Surprises you, does it? Stranger and stranger...\nWait, don't tell me...
MID_EV12_068_m01_028: You can't mean you came from across the sea!
MID_EV12_068_m01_029: Hmm...
MID_EV12_068_m01_001: You did, didn't you? And lived to tell the tale. Well,\nI'll be.
MID_EV12_068_m01_002: From the look of it, you got swept up by a storm...\nand dropped right down in sea-beast territory.
MID_EV12_068_m01_003: And that's how your ship got sunk. After what I've\nseen, I'd put money on it.
MID_EV12_068_m01_004: Wreckage and bodies been washing up all day. Tells\na tale.
MID_EV12_068_m01_005: <NCA>Recall.
MID_EV12_068_m01_006: We locked eyes. The beast grinned.
MID_EV12_068_m01_007: It grinned? The sea beast did? Damn fool! Must be\nseeing things...
MID_EV12_068_m01_008: Well, you may be a fool, but you're a lucky one.
MID_EV12_068_m01_009: Be grateful you're still breathing. Nothing's more\nprecious than that.
MID_EV12_068_m01_010: Looting the wreckage, I see. Industrious of you.\nAnd profitable, perhaps.
MID_EV12_068_m01_011: Hahaha!
MID_EV12_068_m01_012: Pottery, textiles, jewelry... Casks of ale and\nprovender... Strange and wonderful things!
MID_EV12_068_m01_013: The dead washing up here are past caring about any\nof it... But the living have got living to do!
MID_EV12_068_m01_014: Ships all over are bursting with cargo just like this.
MID_EV12_068_m01_015: I haul myself out here every day to sift through what\nwashes up. Make a good living, I do!
MID_EV12_068_m01_016: I may be old, but I keep a roof over my head and\nfood in my belly.
MID_EV12_068_m01_017: It's good that a young feller like you didn't drown.\nWe only get one life to live!
MID_EV12_068_m01_018: Indeed.
MID_EV12_000_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_000_m01_001: There he goes! After him! Catch that priest,\nyou fools!
MID_EV12_000_m01_002: Careful though, careful! He wields strange power...\nI've never seen the like!
MID_EV12_000_m01_003: These beasts! These creatures without shame!\nWhy must they harry me so?
MID_EV12_000_m01_004: This place is more savage and wild yet than Fódlan.
MID_EV12_000_m01_005: Inconceivable that these dogs could run me to\nground... Base cunning! Mere instinct!
MID_EV12_000_m01_006: I! A noble Agarthan!
MID_EV12_000_m01_007: Oh, but there it is...the exquisite tang of\nhumiliation... How it spreads through me!
MID_EV12_000_m01_008: I am vexed beyond bearing! Ah, glorious emotions\nroil my insides... It has been too long!
MID_EV12_000_m01_009: What's he on about? Who's he talking to?
MID_EV12_000_m01_010: A strange one. Must be a foreigner. That means an\nextra-big purse for traveling, boys!
MID_EV12_000_m01_011: Hm?
MID_EV12_000_m01_012: This one... I am certain he is not with them.
MID_EV12_000_m01_013: You! Beautiful stranger! May I enlist your aid?
MID_EV12_000_m01_014: These ruffians assail me. I beg of you...protect me!\nYour reward will be ample!
MID_EV12_000_m01_015: Had a friend, did ya? Well, one corpse, two corpses...\nMakes no difference to me!
MID_EV12_000_m01_016: <NCA>Draw your sword.
MID_EV12_000_m01_017: Will I wring even a drop of pleasure from crossing\nblades with ones such as these?
MID_EV12_000_m01_018: And yet...I thirst. And now warm blood is served in a\ncrude cup.
MID_EV12_000_m01_019: Is that the fell blade Answerer? A Hero's Relic,\nhere in Dagda? But how?
MID_EV12_000_m01_020: You know of my blade?
MID_EV12_000_m01_021: You two! Stick a cork in it!
MID_EV12_000_m01_022: And you, with the sword! You're awfully pretty. Ever\nactually seen a battlefield?
MID_EV12_000_m01_023: Heh heh heh. Two fools who'll soon regret going\nfor a little stroll!
MID_EV12_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_001_m01_001: Mercy, sir! Mercy! Wait!
MID_EV12_001_m01_002: I've got a baby! A wee baby! He's starving! Please!
MID_EV12_001_m01_003: <NCA>Cut him down.
MID_EV12_001_m01_004: Aagh!
MID_EV12_001_m01_005: Strange that I find myself saying this... But I do\nwonder if that was truly necessary.
MID_EV12_001_m01_006: That fool no longer posed a threat. He had lost the\nwill to fight.
MID_EV12_001_m01_007: Once my lust for blood has been roused, it must be\nquieted. He or I—one must fall.
MID_EV12_001_m01_008: Hmm...is that so? Not a very rational way of\nthinking, I must say.
MID_EV12_001_m01_009: May Seiros and the goddess have mercy on the soul\nof this feckless pagan.
MID_EV12_001_m01_010: Ah, but I must thank you, mustn't I? By your hand, I\nyet live.
MID_EV12_001_m01_011: I am Fabio Gil Toro Álvarez, humble missionary of\nthe Church of Seiros.
MID_EV12_001_m01_012: I have traveled to this land, called to spread our\nsublime faith.
MID_EV12_001_m01_013: <NCA>Ask about Fódlan.
MID_EV12_001_m01_014: <NCB>Ask about the sword.
MID_EV12_001_m01_015: <ACA>You hail from Fódlan?
MID_EV12_001_m01_016: <ACA>Yes. As do you, it seems.
MID_EV12_001_m01_017: <ACA>To find a compatriot in this place... I never would\nhave foreseen it.
MID_EV12_001_m01_018: <ACA>It seems the providence of the goddess is more\ngenuine than I had anticipated.
MID_EV12_001_m01_019: <ACB>You know my sword.
MID_EV12_001_m01_020: <ACB>The fell blade Answerer. A relic wielded by Lamine,\none of the 10 Elites of Fódlan.
MID_EV12_001_m01_021: <ACB>Is it not a grievous sin to remove it from that land?
MID_EV12_001_m01_022: <ACB>It was not my intent. I was shipwrecked.
MID_EV12_001_m01_023: I am Dietrich Gregor Lamine.
MID_EV12_001_m01_024: Ah, yes. There it is. You descend from Lamine of\nthe Elites.
MID_EV12_001_m01_025: She was an exquisite woman. That would explain\nyour beauty.
MID_EV12_001_m01_026: My great-grandmother died long ago. I never\nmet her.
MID_EV12_001_m01_027: Yet, you... You speak as though you have.
MID_EV12_001_m01_028: It is merely the common wisdom, is it not? Those in\nmy order speak often of her beauty.
MID_EV12_001_m01_029: {SetColor=Gray}Yes, a lovely specimen. Whenever I set eyes upon\nher, my hand twitched for my scalpel...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_001_m01_030: {SetColor=Gray}How I wrestled with that impulse... Was I drawn to\nher, I wonder?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_001_m01_031: What is this that you're saying?
MID_EV12_001_m01_032: Pardon me, it is nothing. But I must ask, why are\nyou here?
MID_EV12_001_m01_033: My intended destination was the Isle of Eif. The Gáe\nBolg Colosseum. But I was diverted...
MID_EV12_001_m01_034: Gáe Bolg? A brutal, notorious place. What could you\nhope to find there?
MID_EV12_001_m01_035: To seek a fight that would set my body aflame.
MID_EV12_001_m01_036: You seek a fight? But there is said to be a massive\narena here in Dagda.
MID_EV12_001_m01_037: A tournament spanning many moons is to be held,\nI am told.
MID_EV12_001_m01_038: The greatest warriors from across the lands are\ngathering as we speak.
MID_EV12_001_m01_039: Is that so? That is welcome news.
MID_EV12_001_m01_040: {SetColor=Gray}You are but a predatory beast. Like the 10 Elites\nbefore you, your desire for combat animates you.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_001_m01_041: {SetColor=Gray}Driven by the basest of instincts, you thirst for blood.\nWe are stark opposites, you and I...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_001_m01_042: I do owe you my thanks for saving me. Allow me to\nshow you the way.
MID_EV12_001_m01_043: Judge me not by my appearance. I am very\nresourceful.
MID_EV12_001_m01_044: Though one such as I will doubtless suffer under this\nharsh sun. How detestable.
MID_EV12_069_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_069_m01_001: I know that power. Or one much like it... The power\nof the goddess!
MID_EV12_069_m01_002: You clad yourself as we do yet wield the power of\nthese beasts. You are an abomination.
MID_EV12_069_m01_003: What—what do you call yourself?
MID_EV12_069_m01_004: How readily you bare your steel! But no matter.\nI have come here to provide you guidance.
MID_EV12_069_m01_005: We grant you the gift of Divine Sand. As long as you\ncarry this, I will never truly leave your side.
MID_EV12_069_m01_006: The sheer cheek of that one, trying to cut me down!
MID_EV12_069_m01_007: If not for your presence, I would have been sliced\nin twain. 'Tis the last time I intervene for him!
MID_EV12_069_m01_008: What was that?
MID_EV12_069_m01_009: Some sprite that resides in Dagda. One far beyond\nour ken.